# Copy to deploy/spark/.env on the Spark. docker compose reads it automatically.
# Images: vllm, qdrant and mosquitto default to the digest-pinned refs in images.lock (same as the compose
# defaults). Only override one with a tag@sha256:<digest> ref. APP_IMAGE is the locally built version tag;
# install_spark.sh and offline_update.sh set it to warroom-app:<release>. Never :latest.
# VLLM_IMAGE=nvcr.io/nvidia/vllm:<yy.mm>-py3@sha256:<digest>
APP_IMAGE=
HF_CACHE=/opt/warroom/hf
QDRANT_DATA=/opt/warroom/data/qdrant
APP_DATA=/opt/warroom/data/runtime
# Audit log HMAC key and head-anchor mirror, both OUTSIDE APP_DATA (G1). deploy/bin/init-audit-key.sh creates
# them on first install (install_spark.sh runs it) and refuses wrong owners/permissions; an old install whose
# key sat beside the log (APP_DATA/audit.jsonl.key) moves it with deploy/bin/migrate-audit-key.sh first.
# Put the anchor dir on a different disk from APP_DATA when the box has one.
# install_spark.sh writes both (defaults $WARROOM_ROOT/secrets/audit.key and $WARROOM_ROOT/audit-anchor):
# AUDIT_KEY_FILE=/opt/warroom/secrets/audit.key
# AUDIT_ANCHOR_DIR=/opt/warroom/audit-anchor
# /api/sim/* (scenario, speed, step) is OFF on the line. For a demo: deploy/spark-demo/compose-demo.env.
WARROOM_DEMO_CONTROLS=0
# REQUIRED. Supervisor PIN for writes from the factory LAN: the phone page asks for it once and sends it as
# X-Supervisor-Pin on every approval. 8+ random characters, e.g.  openssl rand -base64 9
# The on-box touchscreen (127.0.0.1; the app runs on the host network) needs no PIN.
# install_spark.sh refuses to finish while this is empty or shorter than 8, and compose refuses to start.
# Or pass it at install time:  sudo WARROOM_SUPERVISOR_PIN=... deploy/bin/install_spark.sh
WARROOM_SUPERVISOR_PIN=
# The app listens on every host interface on :8000 (touchscreen on loopback, phone on the LAN).
# Production model server. Control group (page 10): QUANT=fp8 SPEC=off PREFIX_CACHE=0 KV_DTYPE=auto
QUANT=nvfp4
SPEC=dspark
PREFIX_CACHE=1
KV_DTYPE=fp8
MAX_MODEL_LEN=32768
MAX_NUM_SEQS=4
# 0.23 x 128 GB = ~29.4 GB for vLLM -> stack ~48-49 GB (page-9 band 36-50). See vllm-serve.sh.
GPU_MEM_UTIL=0.23
# App
LLM_MODE=llm
SCENARIO=day_loop
SIM_SPEED=1.0
# MQTT (page-10 data path). The broker refuses anonymous clients. The app's own password is generated on first
# start into ${MQTT_DATA}/app.pass unless MQTT_APP_PASSWORD is set. The plant gateway gets user `gateway`
# (publish-only, warroom/telemetry/#) only when MQTT_GATEWAY_PASSWORD is set (12+ chars). To let a real
# gateway reach the broker: MQTT_BIND=<Spark LAN IP> and allow its IP with
#   sudo MQTT_GATEWAYS=<gateway IP> deploy/bin/set_inbound_allow.sh
MQTT_DATA=/opt/warroom/data/mqtt
MQTT_BIND=127.0.0.1
MQTT_APP_PASSWORD=
MQTT_GATEWAY_PASSWORD=
